\NormalTok{                                             MONGE–AMPÈRE MEASURES ON BALANCED POLYHEDRAL SPACES}

\NormalTok{                                                       ANA MARÍA BOTERO, ENRICA MAZZON, AND LÉONARD PILLE–SCHNEIDER}




\NormalTok{arXiv:2603.08664v1 [math.AG] 9 Mar 2026}
\NormalTok{                                                  Abstract. We study classes of convex functions on balanced polyhedral spaces and establish}
\NormalTok{                                                  various structural properties, including a compactness theorem for polyhedrally plurisubharmonic}
\NormalTok{                                                  functions. Using tropical intersection theory, we construct Monge–Ampère measures, first}
\NormalTok{                                                  associated with piecewise affine functions, and then we extend it to polyhedrally plurisubharmonic}
\NormalTok{                                                  functions.}
\NormalTok{                                                     We investigate polyhedral Monge–Ampère equations on balanced polyhedral spaces via a}
\NormalTok{                                                  variational approach, providing sufficient conditions for the existence of solutions as well as explicit}
\NormalTok{                                                  counterexamples. Finally, we relate our framework to non{-}archimedean pluripotential theory and}
\NormalTok{                                                  explore its connection with the non{-}archimedean Monge–Ampère equation.}


