\NormalTok{Definition 2.1 (Rational polyhedron). A rational polyhedron in NR is a subset σ ⊆ NR defined}
\NormalTok{by finitely many affine integral equalities and inequalities, i.e.,}

\NormalTok{                      σ = n ∈ NR | f1 (n) + b1 = . . . = fr (n) + br = 0,}
\NormalTok{                                      fr+1 (n) + br+1 ≥ 0, . . . , fN (n) + bN ≥ 0}
\NormalTok{for some linear forms f1 , . . . , fN ∈ M and bi ∈ Z.}
\NormalTok{    We define}
\NormalTok{      • Nσ,R the linear space spanned by all x − y for x, y ∈ σ;}
\NormalTok{      • Nσ = Nσ,R ∩ N the induced sublattice, and Mσ its dual lattice;}
\NormalTok{      • Vσ,R = x + Nσ,R , x ∈ σ, the smallest affine subspace of NR containing σ;}
\NormalTok{      • the relative interior of σ, denoted by relint(σ) is the interior of σ as a subset of Vσ,R ;}
\NormalTok{      • the dimension of σ as the dimension of Nσ,R .}
\NormalTok{Definition 2.2 (Rational polyhedral complex). A rational polyhedral complex is a finite}
\NormalTok{collection Π of rational polyhedra satisfying two conditions:}
\NormalTok{      • if σ is in Π, then so is any face of σ;}
\NormalTok{      • if σ and σ ′ are in Π, then σ ∩ σ ′ is either empty or a face of both σ and σ ′ .}
\NormalTok{   The polyhedra of Π are called faces and we write τ ≺ σ whenever τ is a face of σ. We denote}
\NormalTok{the set of all k{-}dimensional faces of Π by Π(k) . The union of all faces in Π is denoted |Π| ⊆ NR}
\NormalTok{and called the support of Π.}
\NormalTok{  The dimension of Π is defined as the maximum of the dimensions of the faces of Π, and Π is}
\NormalTok{pure dimensional if every inclusion{-}maximal face in Π has the same dimension.}
\NormalTok{Definition 2.3 (Refinement). A refinement Π′ of a rational polyhedral complex Π is a rational}
\NormalTok{polyhedral complex such that}
\NormalTok{      • |Π′ | = |Π|}
\NormalTok{      • for every σ ′ ∈ Π′ , there exists σ ∈ Π such that σ ′ ⊆ σ;}
\NormalTok{we write Π′ ≥ Π. Two rational polyhedral complexes are equivalent if they admit a common}
\NormalTok{refinement.}
\NormalTok{Definition 2.4 (Rational polyhedral space).}
\NormalTok{      • Let X ⊆ NR be a topological space. A rational polyhedral complex Π is a rational polyhedral}
\NormalTok{        structure on X if |Π| = X.}
\NormalTok{      • A polyhedral space X ⊆ NR is a topological space together with an equivalence class of}
\NormalTok{        rational polyhedral structures on X.}
\NormalTok{      • A polyhedral space X is of dimension d (respectively of pure dimension d) if some (and}
\NormalTok{        hence any) representative of the equivalence class of rational polyhedral structures on X has}
\NormalTok{        dimension d (respectively pure dimension d).}

