\section{Reproducibility and proof
limits}\label{reproducibility-and-proof-limits}

The following are exact finite observations for the stated input germs
only. \texttt{diagnostics.py} uses Fraction arithmetic and evaluates
formula (D) on every product facet at each stage. On a primitive
pair-plane ray (p,q), Bezout integers give an integral normal (-v,u)
with pu+qv=1, whose sign is selected by the adjacent cone determinant.
It maps this normal through the original primitive axes, retains the
common tangential correction, and checks that the weighted normal sum
lies in each actual facet tangent. The algorithm does not insert a top
mass: it computes the first, second and every later divisor directly. It
separately evaluates every surviving mixed ordering and a repeated
exhausted factor. These local finite calculations do not enumerate
global envelopes or prove the complete contact integral.

